{
  "id": "temporal-coherence",
  "term": "temporal coherence",
  "definition": "Temporal coherence is the tendency for different parts of a sound from the same source to change in strength together over time. In hearing, the brain uses these shared timing patterns to group related sounds into one stream and to separate them from other sounds with different patterns.",
